From 40bbfd10f48bec66eed611bb83f592b00d405926 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 22:29:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add evaluation layer: statistics, auditor calibration, anchor
 drift suite

Ports the pure statistics from the bench eval harness into src/core and wires
them to two questions this repo could not previously answer: does the auditor
agree with a human, and has it silently changed its mind.

- src/core/evalStats.ts        kappa, Gwet AC1, exact McNemar, paired t, Wilson,
                               power with a floor so a large gap cannot report
                               that two items would have been enough
- src/core/auditCalibration.ts per-dimension agreement between auditProtocol and
                               human labels; excludes what the auditor declined
                               to assess rather than counting it as agreement
- src/core/sopRubric.ts        the SOP-drafting rubric as typed data; hard fails
                               gate rather than deduct
- tests/auditAnchor.test.ts    five frozen fixtures plus a recorded baseline;
                               catches auditor drift, not model drift
- tests/sopQuality.test.ts     skips until a real golden set exists

85 new tests. Reference values computed independently with SciPy, not recorded
from this implementation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XrLkHSCmvvz4sDsZDVpGhr
